@Tap_to_Ride_v2.Server_HostAddress = http://localhost:5058

### 1. Post a batch of two trips for rider-001 (R12 + R12 = R24)
POST {{Tap_to_Ride_v2.Server_HostAddress}}/api/batches
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "batchId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
  "trips": [
    { "tripId": "t1", "riderId": "rider-001", "fareCents": 1200, "takenAt": "2026-09-18T06:15:00Z", "signature": "x" },
    { "tripId": "t2", "riderId": "rider-001", "fareCents": 1200, "takenAt": "2026-09-18T06:45:00Z", "signature": "x" }
  ]
}

### 2. Post the exact same batch again — the idempotency test
POST {{Tap_to_Ride_v2.Server_HostAddress}}/api/batches
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "batchId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
  "trips": [
    { "tripId": "t1", "riderId": "rider-001", "fareCents": 1200, "takenAt": "2026-09-18T06:15:00Z", "signature": "x" },
    { "tripId": "t2", "riderId": "rider-001", "fareCents": 1200, "takenAt": "2026-09-18T06:45:00Z", "signature": "x" }
  ]
}

### 3. Confirm the charge is R24.00 (2400), not R48.00 — request 2 must not have doubled it
GET {{Tap_to_Ride_v2.Server_HostAddress}}/api/riders/rider-001/charge

### 4. Push rider-001 past the R50 daily cap with a second batch
POST {{Tap_to_Ride_v2.Server_HostAddress}}/api/batches
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "batchId": "22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222",
  "trips": [
    { "tripId": "t3", "riderId": "rider-001", "fareCents": 1200, "takenAt": "2026-09-18T07:00:00Z", "signature": "x" },
    { "tripId": "t4", "riderId": "rider-001", "fareCents": 1200, "takenAt": "2026-09-18T07:10:00Z", "signature": "x" },
    { "tripId": "t5", "riderId": "rider-001", "fareCents": 1200, "takenAt": "2026-09-18T07:20:00Z", "signature": "x" }
  ]
}

### 5. Confirm the cap held at R50.00 (5000), not the raw R60.00 sum
GET {{Tap_to_Ride_v2.Server_HostAddress}}/api/riders/rider-001/charge

### 6. Check that every individual trip is still there, itemised
GET {{Tap_to_Ride_v2.Server_HostAddress}}/api/riders/rider-001/trips
